WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.070
You have three layers of resources you have to ask yourself:

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:07.877
how much I have left today? From easy to hard.

00:00:07.997 --> 00:00:11.410
The first layer is time. It's easy to think:

00:00:11.471 --> 00:00:14.931
I still have three hours until I wrap up the day,

00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:18.812
and I have a critical task that I have to finish.

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:21.252
Easy. Just take two hours, so I can finish them.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.664
I don't have enough time for this for today, so I'll push it tomorrow.

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:28.131
The second layer is about thinking.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.336
You have three hours left. It doesn't mean you can think for three hours.

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:34.636
Nobody can think for eight hours a day,

00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:37.098
even if you have 8 working hours a day.

00:00:37.207 --> 00:00:40.507
Do I have to think this problem, make a decision today,

00:00:40.527 --> 00:00:41.975
or is that a tomorrow problem?

00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:44.798
The third layer is emotional resource.

00:00:44.898 --> 00:00:48.773
It's the hard one. It's hard to gauge. A lot of people don't even realize it.

00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:53.078
Because hard conversations, performance management conversations,

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:56.449
escalations, conflicts, urgencies,

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:59.039
they all cost you emotional resources.

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:01.697
So this is the time you ask yourself:

00:01:01.746 --> 00:01:04.849
I do have time today. I do have thinking power today.

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:08.659
Do I still have enough emotional resources today?

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.540
Maybe some of the things couldn't be done today,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.382
simply because you don't have enough emotional reserve.

00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:18.427
So these are the three layers of things you ask yourself,

00:01:18.447 --> 00:01:21.527
and you can make better decisions at the right time.
